Package: popcorn
Title: Population-Scale Personalized Coexpression Network Estimation
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Shuchen", "Yan", email = "syan58@wisc.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kris", "Sankaran", role = "aut"),
    person("Sündüz", "Keleş", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates reliable, donor-specific gene co-expression
    correlations from population-scale single-cell RNA-seq data. POPCORN
    first fits a covariate-adjusted marginal model to correct technical
    and compositional noise within each donor's own cells, then applies
    a random-effects variance decomposition that separates genuine
    between-donor heterogeneity from sampling noise at each gene pair,
    adaptively shrinking noisy donor-level estimates toward the global
    correlation using information borrowed jointly across donors.
